l","question":"If $y=f(x)$ and $\\mathrm{d}y=f'(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, what does the factor $f'(x)$ describe?","options":["The exact change $\\Delta y$ for a small $\\mathrm{d}x$","The average slope of $f$ over $[x,x+\\mathrm{d}x]$","The tangent slope turning $\\mathrm{d}x$ into $\\mathrm{d}y$","The relative change $\\mathrm{d}y/y$ per unit $\\mathrm{d}x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dd63afa7e40315b8a6126236","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x) = x^2$, what is $\\mathrm{d}f(x)$?","options":["$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = 2x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = x^2\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = \\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = 0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5292564637f61072111a7c27","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x) = \\sin x$, what is $\\mathrm{d}f(x)$?","options":["$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = \\sin x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = -\\sin x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = \\cos x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x) = x\\,\\mathrm{d}x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7c07ed15486bed579c859d00","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which property of the differential holds?","options":["It depends quadratically on the increment $\\mathrm{d}x$.","It exists whenever $f$ is continuous.","It is the same object as the function value $f(x)$.","It depends linearly on the increment $\\mathrm{d}x$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"38b73ef2c6d699eb0ff66256","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does the differential provide near a point?","options":["The exact function value at every other input","A linear approximation of the function near that point","A quadratic approximation using the curvature at that point","The average rate of change of the function over an interval"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3dde4fab2c6b3749b6291699","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $f'(a) = 3$ and $\\mathrm{d}x = 0.1$, what is $\\mathrm{d}f(a)$?","options":["$0.3$","$3.1$","$30$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"340b5363df31d4e4c79e224c","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $f(x) = x^2$ at $x = 3$, what is $\\mathrm{d}f(3)$?","options":["$3\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$9\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}x^2$","$6\\,\\mathrm{d}x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3d3b9f190f5a0f6ac5ad65fd","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_009","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which assumption guarantees the existence of a differential at $x$?","options":["$f$ is differentiable at $x$.","$f$ is continuous at $x$, with no derivative assumption.","$x$ is outside the domain.","$f(x) = 0$ only."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fb1f6c8728e85ae936dd35f5","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_010","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement correctly distinguishes $\\mathrm{d}f(x)$ from $f(x)$?","options":["$\\mathrm{d}f(x)$ is $f'(x)$, the derivative alone","$\\mathrm{d}f(x)$ is the tangent value $f(x)+f'(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x)$ is the exact change $f(x+\\mathrm{d}x)-f(x)$","$\\mathrm{d}f(x)$ is $f'(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, not $f(x)$ itself"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7641bc8b46665bbc0feb7962","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353